## Files Modified
- `pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated with latest dependency resolutions

## Files Already Configured (No Changes Needed)
- `package.json` - Already contains `@vercel/speed-insights` dependency
- `app/layout.tsx` - Already has SpeedInsights component properly integrated

## Implementation Details

The implementation matches the official documentation exactly:
```typescript
import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next';

export default function RootLayout({ children }) {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        {children}
        <SpeedInsights />
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```

## Next Steps for User

To see Speed Insights data:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard for your project
3. Visit your deployed site to generate real user metrics
4. View insights in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights tab

## Notes
- The SpeedInsights component automatically detects the Vercel environment and will only collect data when deployed on Vercel
- No environment variables are required for basic setup
- The component has minimal performance impact and uses the Web Vitals API
- Speed Insights is already integrated alongside `@vercel/analytics` which is also present in the project
